{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update22.json\",\"summary\":\"Requested the execution of the completed basis for the Node-wrapper question (successor of c3dd9a52a0c44b21af5b3204cf642efb-experiment). The corrected harness now also measures the leadership-change restore path, and the native run shows the whole arc on a conforming prefix: before the removal Propose returns no error in 0ms with the leader's log index at 2; after the re-add, with the leader's configuration containing node 2 again and the node still knowing leader 1 in term 1, Propose returns only when its 300ms deadline fires with the leader's log index unchanged at 4; then the wrapped node campaigns and wins (status StateLeader at term 2, known leader itself, commit 5) and the same Propose call returns no error in 0ms with its commit index advancing from 5 to 6. The basis therefore carries nine comparisons - the two controls, the two premises on the witness event, the two violated witness assertions, and three restore comparisons (campaign state StateLeader, no error on the repeated call, commit advanced) - with prerequisites chained through the shared scenario field and each alias matched by exactly one event. Note on the earlier failure of this control: with the corrected prefix the wrapped node's log is consistent and the election is winnable, which locates the previous rejection in the tainted prefix rather than in the question. Incomplete: the receipt for this basis is outstanding; the account update itself (interpretation) has not been written yet, so the recorded account still cites the previous receipt and lists the restore path as unmeasured.\"}"}}
